flickos-theme: where the source comes from
==========================================

src/ is the GTK 3 and GTK 4 part of arc-theme 20221218 (the version of Debian
trixie and forky; upstream https://github.com/jnsh/arc-theme):

  src/gtk-3.0/sass, src/gtk-4.0/sass   common/gtk-3.0/sass and common/gtk-4.0/sass
  src/assets                           the PNG assets, taken from the
                                       gtk.gresource of Debian's arc-theme
                                       20221218-1 (GTK 3 and GTK 4 use the
                                       same 168 files)
  src/COPYING, src/AUTHORS             upstream's

build.sh compiles the Sass as arc-theme's meson build does (the templates
gtk.scss.in with transparency on, sassc --style compact) and puts the result
and the assets into one gtk.gresource per theme folder.

FlickOS's changes to the Sass are marked "FlickOS:" in the files
(grep -rn "FlickOS:" src/), made as docs/design/flickos-seamless-2x.md
(ADR-2X-1) says. They are shapes only; Arc's colors are unchanged:

  - corners: 6 px on controls, rows' frames and tabs, 8 px on popovers, menus,
    dialogs, the window and the header bar (arc-theme wrote them as literals);
  - $header_height (_colors.scss, 32 px, !default): the header bar's
    min-height, and its buttons and entries are sized from it;
  - $side_bg, $side_fg, $side_border (_colors.scss): the sidebars of Thunar
    and the file chooser; equal to the window's colors in the light theme, Arc's
    dark sidebar colors in the dark one;
  - header bar buttons with a text, packed in the bar itself (wdisplays'
    Cancel and Apply): a margin of ($header_height - 22px) / 2 and, unless
    they are action buttons, Arc's button outline (`> button.text-button`
    at the end of _common.scss);
  - GTK 4: the same radii and header height ($header_radius 8 px).

src/frame-dark.css and src/frame-light.css are FlickOS's: the window frame for
client-side decorated windows (GTK 3; Thunar's header bar), which labwc's
theme can't reach. Their colors follow labwc's border colors, and tools/check-look.py
compares them and the header bar's colors with the title bar's.

To update to a new arc-theme: unpack its orig tarball, replace the Sass,
re-apply the changes by looking for "FlickOS:" in the old files, rebuild the
assets list from the new gresource, and run the tests.

Not here: the labwc themes of the same names stay in flickos-settings
(/usr/share/themes/FlickOS-Arc*/labwc); both packages put files in the folder.
